WEBVTT

01:04.230 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:09.694 --> 01:13.031
DAUGHTER OF YANG GWAN-SIK AND OH AE-SUN
YANG GEUM-MYEONG! ACCEPTED TO SNU!

01:20.163 --> 01:23.583
'88 SEOUL OLYMPICS CELEBRATION
ADVANCED CITIZENS! ADVANCED STREETS!

01:23.666 --> 01:25.627
Who cares
if you're from the Olympics?

01:25.710 --> 01:27.712
Haenyeo do more than Olympians every day!

01:27.796 --> 01:29.214
For the haenyeo,

01:29.297 --> 01:32.133
their "Olympics"
was simply making ends meet.

01:32.217 --> 01:35.386
Please, everyone, calm down.
If you'd just let us explain.

01:35.470 --> 01:37.680
And the Olympic events
they competed in

01:37.764 --> 01:39.974
were as grand as they were cruel.

01:40.725 --> 01:41.976
Games without medals,

01:42.560 --> 01:43.394
pensions,

01:43.978 --> 01:45.105
or retirement.

01:45.688 --> 01:48.024
What the hell are you ruining
our business for?

01:48.108 --> 01:50.902
Why? Go do your Olympics
if that's what you want.

01:50.985 --> 01:53.363
-Why do we have to sacrifice for it?
-Oh God.

01:53.947 --> 01:55.448
Who are you trying to punish here?

01:55.532 --> 01:58.201
Who ever saw a conch
protesting the Olympics?

01:58.284 --> 01:59.661
Or a fish blocking the roads?

01:59.744 --> 02:02.580
All right! Enough!

02:02.664 --> 02:04.624
Seriously! I've had enough.
We need to get through!

02:04.707 --> 02:06.376
How many times do I have to tell you?

02:06.459 --> 02:09.129
The Olympic torch
will be passing right through here!

02:09.212 --> 02:11.798
Americans are going to watch this
on their TVs!

02:11.881 --> 02:13.842
We can't let anyone see that.

02:13.925 --> 02:17.387
All these disgusting intestines
and the smell of fish guts here?

02:17.470 --> 02:19.597
Are you stupid or what?
Can you smell your TV?

02:19.681 --> 02:23.143
We have orders from the government
to clean up anything unsightly.

02:23.226 --> 02:24.727
That's an order!

02:24.811 --> 02:25.770
That's an order!

02:25.854 --> 02:27.730
-Why you little…
-Unsightly, eh?

02:27.814 --> 02:30.984
Now I've heard it all.
You're going to take away our livelihoods

02:31.067 --> 02:34.195
just to serve some Americans
thousands of miles away?

02:34.279 --> 02:36.739
Does that make
any kind of sense to you at all?

02:36.823 --> 02:39.159
Is that the American way
of doing business?

02:39.242 --> 02:41.953
Trampling the poor
by taking the food out of our mouths!

02:42.036 --> 02:42.996
I can't take this.

02:43.079 --> 02:45.206
Oh, come on,
you're no crusaders for justice.

02:45.290 --> 02:47.500
You're just fish-sellers like I am.

02:47.584 --> 02:50.044
I think we can all handle
a little loss for the greater good.

02:50.128 --> 02:52.046
Now stop messing things up!

02:52.130 --> 02:54.591
I know what happened.
They paid you off, didn't they?

02:55.300 --> 02:58.094
What? 'Cause I don't have
enough money yet, you think?

02:58.178 --> 02:59.554
How much was it, huh?

02:59.637 --> 03:02.557
How much did they pay you
for our blood, sweat, and tears?

03:03.183 --> 03:04.642
You call yourself "chief"?

03:04.726 --> 03:07.228
Maybe you would have some manners
if you had gone to school.

03:07.312 --> 03:08.938
Explain it to us again!

03:09.022 --> 03:11.107
The Olympic torch will pass through
for a few minutes,

03:11.191 --> 03:13.985
and just for that,
you wanna take away our income?

03:14.068 --> 03:15.862
What kind of law is that?

03:15.945 --> 03:17.697
-Oh, please. What about it?
-Go away!

03:17.780 --> 03:19.282
What do you know about the law?

03:19.365 --> 03:21.326
Oh Ae-sun!

03:21.409 --> 03:22.869
Where's Ae-sun?

03:22.952 --> 03:26.164
Go get our deputy chief.
She finished high school.

03:26.247 --> 03:28.374
Finished high school?

03:28.458 --> 03:31.419
-She didn't even graduate.
-Well, she went at least.

03:32.045 --> 03:34.380
Where is our deputy chief?

03:34.464 --> 03:37.133
-She would know exactly what to say!
-Ae-sun!

03:37.217 --> 03:39.469
What are you shouting about
Ae-sun for?

03:39.552 --> 03:41.930
It's not like she can do anything.

03:42.013 --> 03:45.350
I want you to explain
how not selling our fish helps the nation.

03:45.433 --> 03:47.727
God, can't you see this doesn't matter?

03:48.311 --> 03:50.271
If North Korea decides
to ruin our Olympics

03:50.355 --> 03:53.316
and bursts the Mount Kumgang dam,
all of Seoul will be flooded.

03:53.399 --> 03:56.027
Even the 63 Building
would be under the sea.

03:56.110 --> 03:57.987
Don't you follow the news?

03:58.071 --> 04:00.323
Don't you understand?
It's for the greater good.

04:00.406 --> 04:03.701
Compared to history,
your little lives don't matter at all.

04:03.785 --> 04:05.578
Yes, they do. Yes, they do.

04:05.662 --> 04:07.622
-You bet your ass they matter.
-Oh, it's hopeless.

04:10.124 --> 04:12.710
Do you know how riots get started?

04:12.794 --> 04:15.546
If you kick over a dog's bowl of food,

04:15.630 --> 04:18.466
it's gonna start shitting
all over the place!

04:18.549 --> 04:19.759
-Is that what you want?
-Let go.

04:19.842 --> 04:21.052
Is that what you want?

04:21.636 --> 04:22.553
Huh?

04:22.637 --> 04:23.680
-Ae-sun!
-No, no, no.

04:23.763 --> 04:25.556
-That's not what I want.
-Ae-sun!

04:25.640 --> 04:28.059
Hey! She's right there.
Right there. Here she is.

04:28.142 --> 04:30.144
-Ae-sun, there you are.
-She'll tell you.

04:30.228 --> 04:31.312
Well?

04:32.021 --> 04:33.690
Wait. Deputy.

04:35.650 --> 04:36.567
Deputy.

04:50.957 --> 04:53.084
She's not gonna start shitting here,
is she?

04:58.006 --> 04:59.007
Hey, get up.

05:00.633 --> 05:02.385
There's an outcry with no sound

05:03.261 --> 05:04.387
What's that?

05:04.470 --> 05:07.265
Lashed by the season's bitter scourge

05:07.348 --> 05:09.809
You're embarrassing yourself.
Stop making a scene.

05:11.477 --> 05:14.188
-If you get fed up with me and--
-Hey, someone get a forklift.

05:14.272 --> 05:15.398
Then run me over!

05:15.481 --> 05:18.151
Hey, this is a gangster.
She's not a high school graduate.

05:18.234 --> 05:21.821
The only gangsters here are the ones
stealing people's livelihoods.

05:21.904 --> 05:23.781
What? You can't be serious!

05:23.865 --> 05:24.824
Bring it on!

05:24.907 --> 05:27.035
Oh, now I'm really getting pissed off!

05:27.118 --> 05:28.411
Bring it on!

05:28.494 --> 05:30.663
Just tell them to pack it up! Come on!

05:30.747 --> 05:32.623
I said, bring it on!

05:34.459 --> 05:36.085
Do your worst!

05:42.675 --> 05:45.553
My goodness,
what happened to the bookworm?

05:46.137 --> 05:47.638
Well, I know what. I know what.

05:47.722 --> 05:49.474
Life happened, that's what.

05:49.974 --> 05:51.225
I don't believe it.

05:52.810 --> 05:53.978
Damn it.

05:54.062 --> 05:55.688
Hey, Bu Sang-gil.

05:55.772 --> 05:56.689
A FRUITFUL FALL

05:56.773 --> 05:58.941
You better compensate us
for the day of lost sales!

05:59.442 --> 06:01.444
OPPOSITION PARTIES FAIL TO AGREE
ON SINGLE CANDIDACY

06:01.527 --> 06:03.363
Politics is as fickle as the wind,
isn't it?

06:03.988 --> 06:07.575
The whole town is talking about
how you could be the next village chief.

06:07.658 --> 06:10.703
Please. I told you.
I have no interest in politics.

06:10.787 --> 06:14.707
That's what you types always say.
Then, lo and behold, you end up running.

06:15.583 --> 06:17.543
This election is between
a government stooge

06:17.627 --> 06:18.753
and real fighters like us.

06:18.836 --> 06:21.172
If we let
that treacherous idiot of a chief

06:21.255 --> 06:23.549
win with all the money
from the Olympic bureaucrats,

06:23.633 --> 06:25.635
then all of us haenyeo are screwed.

06:25.718 --> 06:28.679
If he wants to get called "chief,"
he should be acting like one, right?

06:28.763 --> 06:30.723
I hate how he calls you "deputy"
all the time.

06:31.349 --> 06:33.976
It's all, "Hey, deputy" this,
"deputy" that!

06:34.060 --> 06:34.977
"Hey, deputy!"

06:35.061 --> 06:38.106
-That's how he says it.
-She can't stand being a number two.

06:38.189 --> 06:40.316
If a dog like him can be the chief,
then why not her?

06:40.400 --> 06:43.236
Let's make a haenyeo's daughter
village chief.

06:43.319 --> 06:45.905
Will you cut it out?
I have no interest in politics.

06:45.988 --> 06:47.323
I told you that.

06:47.407 --> 06:48.324
Oh?

06:48.408 --> 06:50.576
So we should just ignore

06:50.660 --> 06:51.869
what your husband wants?

06:53.913 --> 06:55.665
Wow, this is a first.

06:56.666 --> 07:00.086
It looks like our captain
is on the campaign trail.

07:00.670 --> 07:03.756
All right, you gave us snacks.
Who should we vote for?

07:04.507 --> 07:07.176
We took the bribe, Captain.
Talk to us.

07:07.844 --> 07:08.678
Well,

07:10.263 --> 07:12.265
I don't say this because she's my wife.

07:12.890 --> 07:16.185
She has been a natural leader.
She's been guiding us often.

07:16.269 --> 07:17.478
I witnessed it myself.

07:19.647 --> 07:24.026
More than that, she's smart. In fact,
I've never in my life met anyone smarter.

07:24.110 --> 07:25.194
That's my honest opinion.

07:25.278 --> 07:28.406
Sure, she was smart enough
to make you captain.

07:35.663 --> 07:36.873
Hey.

07:36.956 --> 07:38.708
Let's be frank here.

07:38.791 --> 07:42.003
Are you really okay with
Ae-sun being the village chief?

07:42.712 --> 07:46.507
Your wife would be the first female
village chief Dodong-ri has ever had.

07:46.591 --> 07:48.092
What happens to you?

07:48.176 --> 07:51.387
I'm not sure if that's
respectable for a man.

07:51.471 --> 07:54.182
Sure, she'd be the first, but so would I.

07:54.265 --> 07:56.684
If Ae-sun becomes
the first female chief of the village,

07:56.767 --> 07:59.729
then that would make me
the first husband of the chief.

08:00.688 --> 08:01.689
That's respectable.

08:01.772 --> 08:03.900
I wouldn't even
have to do anything at all.

08:03.983 --> 08:05.985
Well, just slow down, huh?

08:06.068 --> 08:08.279
You're making the rest of us men look bad.

08:08.362 --> 08:11.199
Our captain's dreams
sure sound different from ours.

08:13.826 --> 08:16.454
Here, they just came out with this brand.

08:20.124 --> 08:23.211
All of it. I'm going to be
the chief of the fishing village,

08:23.294 --> 08:26.005
and then I'll be president
five times in a row.

08:29.300 --> 08:30.676
When you grow up, what will you be?

08:30.760 --> 08:32.512
What are you asking him for?

08:32.595 --> 08:34.597
-Goodness.
-Oh my.

08:34.680 --> 08:36.098
The First Gentleman.

08:37.600 --> 08:38.768
The First Gentleman.

08:39.685 --> 08:40.895
Well…

08:40.978 --> 08:42.813
What is it, First Lady?

08:43.397 --> 08:44.315
Those drinks,

08:45.566 --> 08:47.610
there are actually
real, fresh bananas in there.

08:47.693 --> 08:49.320
This is the best quality, you guys.

08:51.531 --> 08:52.490
I see you like it.

08:55.284 --> 08:58.246
It's all right,
but this banana milk is nothing.

08:58.829 --> 09:01.916
That bigwig you're running against
is giving away pork.

09:01.999 --> 09:03.167
Who doesn't love pork?

09:03.251 --> 09:05.836
Listen up.
This isn't just any old pork.

09:06.420 --> 09:08.422
This is Jeju black pork.

09:08.506 --> 09:09.924
Oh yes.

09:10.007 --> 09:11.926
From Jeju Island black pig.

09:12.009 --> 09:14.804
Make sure everyone gets a double serving
of this premium meat.

09:14.887 --> 09:17.348
Premium? This is what we always serve.

09:17.431 --> 09:20.810
Listen up, everybody.
Don't think I have an ulterior motive.

09:20.893 --> 09:24.105
Really, I'm not doing this
for money or honor.

09:24.647 --> 09:26.732
My only concern is, and always has been,

09:27.900 --> 09:31.237
"How can I give the folks
in our village something good?"

09:31.320 --> 09:33.990
"How can I give folks something to enjoy?"

09:34.073 --> 09:35.491
Can I have some water?

09:35.575 --> 09:37.201
-Garlic, please.
-Water, please.

09:37.285 --> 09:40.830
Could you at least listen to me
when I'm talking to you? Sheesh.

09:41.330 --> 09:43.708
I don't know why
you squeezed us all in here

09:43.791 --> 09:45.585
just to feed us a morsel of pork.

09:46.627 --> 09:49.422
Finish your plate, Grandma.
Then you can order more.

09:50.298 --> 09:52.758
You don't look like one of my supporters,
but here you are.

09:52.842 --> 09:54.927
She's right. You're barely feeding them.

09:55.011 --> 09:57.305
You're frugal, I'll give you that.

09:57.388 --> 09:59.515
So, think about it.

10:00.141 --> 10:03.185
Oh Ae-sun has basically
no history to speak of

10:03.769 --> 10:07.607
whereas my family built this town
and continues to serve!

10:07.690 --> 10:10.943
I ordered soda an hour ago.
When are you gonna serve that?

10:11.027 --> 10:13.195
Not everyone is born a leader,

10:13.696 --> 10:16.449
which is exactly why
we should carefully examine

10:16.532 --> 10:19.410
each candidate's past to check
for any issues or family problems.

10:19.493 --> 10:20.745
What family problems?

10:20.828 --> 10:23.372
I heard Gwan-sik
got an official commendation.

10:23.873 --> 10:26.417
-Do you have any of those?
-It's not a commendation, all right?

10:26.500 --> 10:27.710
It's a plaque of appreciation.

10:27.793 --> 10:30.212
I could get a dozen of those things,
no problem.

10:31.130 --> 10:32.506
But you don't have any.

10:32.590 --> 10:34.508
Have you ever saved anyone from drowning?

10:34.592 --> 10:36.927
Stop talking over me! Hush.

10:37.011 --> 10:39.221
You should learn to listen
when someone is talking to you.

10:39.305 --> 10:42.475
All you ladies just want to butt in
the first chance you get, aren't you?

10:42.558 --> 10:45.603
What about you? Why don't you
listen to me about that soda?

10:46.646 --> 10:48.105
Now, as I was saying,

10:48.189 --> 10:51.275
that family isn't exactly
a shining example of behavior.

10:51.984 --> 10:55.321
At 18, they stole high-end jewelry
and ran off together.

10:55.404 --> 10:58.908
-Their daughter was conceived like that.
-She's at Seoul National University.

10:58.991 --> 11:00.618
Well, the second child is a rotten egg!

11:01.661 --> 11:05.414
I don't wanna speak ill
of other people's kids, but him?

11:06.999 --> 11:09.669
-It's hard to say anything good.
-Okay, then don't.

11:09.752 --> 11:11.295
Bring my soda instead.

11:11.379 --> 11:13.547
I'm saying the apple
never falls far from the tree.

11:13.631 --> 11:16.717
When you start with parents like those,
what do you expect to come out?

11:17.343 --> 11:18.719
It's in their genes!

11:21.597 --> 11:25.184
DODONG-RI FISHING CO-OP DEPUTY CHIEF
MOTHER OF YANG EUN-MYEONG

11:25.267 --> 11:26.936
DODONG-RI FISHING CO-OP CHIEF

11:35.569 --> 11:37.738
Did you come here
from the hair salon?

11:41.200 --> 11:42.410
Take that off.

11:44.495 --> 11:47.832
So how many other student officers are
bringing their mothers to school today?

11:50.501 --> 11:52.503
I can't believe they made you PE leader.

11:52.586 --> 11:54.630
Of all people.

11:55.214 --> 11:56.632
It's just too funny.

11:59.301 --> 12:00.678
Oh goodness.

12:00.761 --> 12:03.973
I'm sure the other mothers
will have so many questions for me.

12:04.056 --> 12:07.059
Like how your sister made it
into Seoul University.

12:07.143 --> 12:09.478
I'll be they'll wanna know
what our secret was.

12:09.562 --> 12:11.188
About that.

12:12.815 --> 12:14.525
It's at 4:00, right? Let's go.

12:15.693 --> 12:18.237
-Mom.
-Ooh, I hope I'm not too early.

12:18.904 --> 12:21.240
-Mom, wait.
-Is this where all the mothers are?

12:21.323 --> 12:22.700
There are no other mothers.

12:24.076 --> 12:27.288
Why? I thought
this was for all the student officers.

12:27.913 --> 12:30.207
-It's actually just for us.
-What?

12:33.377 --> 12:35.421
Hello, sir. I can't tell you how--

12:35.504 --> 12:36.964
No need to come in, ma'am.

12:37.047 --> 12:38.632
-Follow me outside.
-Huh?

12:39.800 --> 12:40.760
To the parking lot?

12:51.562 --> 12:54.023
Apparently, I drive an Onata now!

12:56.525 --> 13:00.112
And another teacher just discovered
he's driving a Hyundai Pon!

13:00.196 --> 13:03.449
The students believe if they get
the initials to their dream colleges,

13:03.532 --> 13:05.576
it will help with their odds
of getting in.

13:05.659 --> 13:07.161
Is that the way your sister did it?

13:07.745 --> 13:10.080
And… and he's not just
stealing these letters.

13:10.164 --> 13:11.540
He's actually selling them off!

13:13.584 --> 13:16.837
Ma'am, I shouldn't have to tell you
how serious this is.

13:16.921 --> 13:18.881
Just look at the principal's car!

13:19.381 --> 13:21.467
Have you ever heard of a Tellar GX?

13:23.427 --> 13:25.805
I've been teaching for more than 20 years.

13:25.888 --> 13:28.224
And in that time,
no student has turned my car

13:28.307 --> 13:30.476
into an Onata until Yang Eun-myeong!

13:31.060 --> 13:31.894
I'm sorry, sir.

13:31.977 --> 13:34.230
He only comes to school
for his side hustles.

13:34.730 --> 13:36.357
He's certainly good with his hands.

13:37.441 --> 13:40.820
He's always scheming. Whether it's cutting
a set of ten bus tickets into eleven

13:40.903 --> 13:42.488
for a profit of 50 won

13:42.571 --> 13:44.448
or playing the coin flipping game

13:44.532 --> 13:46.283
and stealing the coin
when no one's looking.

13:47.284 --> 13:49.161
School isn't a business!

13:49.245 --> 13:52.331
It's not a job.
Only the teachers should be getting paid.

13:53.332 --> 13:56.001
He probably makes more money
at this school than I do.

13:57.253 --> 13:58.212
I'm sorry, sir.

13:58.295 --> 14:02.132
You cared so much for your daughter
that you've completely neglected your son.

14:02.800 --> 14:05.469
Do you even know what kind of students
he's hanging out with?

14:19.984 --> 14:22.027
That's right, stay away from me.

14:23.696 --> 14:25.114
I don't wanna hear a word.

14:27.908 --> 14:30.703
"All the mothers will be there."
Well, you got me.

14:31.745 --> 14:33.455
What's with these little schemes anyway?

14:33.956 --> 14:35.916
Why can't you just study
like you're supposed to?

14:36.000 --> 14:37.918
Why are you so obsessed with money?

14:38.002 --> 14:41.046
You know, I was never embarrassed
at school when your sister was here.

14:41.130 --> 14:43.632
But now I can't look
your teacher in the eye!

14:44.675 --> 14:46.176
Stop hitting the trees!

14:50.014 --> 14:51.515
What's going on with you?

14:51.599 --> 14:52.808
Where did we go wrong?

14:52.892 --> 14:55.394
I said we'd be happy
if you're even half like your sister.

14:55.477 --> 14:57.062
Was that too much to ask?

14:57.146 --> 14:59.189
Right, if I'm not like her,
you can't be chief.

14:59.273 --> 15:01.525
My bad genes are holding you back.

15:01.609 --> 15:04.445
No, that's--
Where did you hear that?

15:04.528 --> 15:07.364
-Bu Sang-gil, that jerk.
-You don't have to lie.

15:08.407 --> 15:10.409
You've always loved her more than me.

15:33.724 --> 15:36.936
The son might be trouble,
but her daughter is a scholar.

15:37.019 --> 15:39.521
Education isn't everything,
is it?

15:39.605 --> 15:42.191
Can education change who her mother is?

15:42.691 --> 15:45.611
Sure, she's at that fancy school…

15:46.820 --> 15:50.324
…but she'll throw it all away
for some boy first chance she gets.

15:50.407 --> 15:52.576
CELEBRATING DIRECT PRESIDENTIAL
ELECTION SYSTEM

15:52.660 --> 15:56.789
♪ That my life would change forever… ♪

15:59.249 --> 16:01.919
He's always coming to pick her up.
Is that her boyfriend?

16:02.002 --> 16:03.337
I guess he's well-off.

16:03.420 --> 16:06.423
Even if he is, how can a college student
drive that kind of car?

16:07.216 --> 16:08.801
You know, something's up with her.

16:09.843 --> 16:12.972
I saw it on TV.
Lots of college girls are escorts.

16:13.639 --> 16:16.809
They get paid to go on dates
with older guys and pretend to like them.

16:17.434 --> 16:20.104
Ju-gyeong, listen,
you gotta watch your mouth.

16:20.187 --> 16:23.107
♪ Real fantasy ♪

16:24.149 --> 16:27.611
♪ Illusions are a common thing ♪

16:27.695 --> 16:30.823
♪ I try to live in dreams ♪

16:30.906 --> 16:32.241
♪ It seems as… ♪

16:32.825 --> 16:34.660
He's gotta be from
the US, right?

16:35.244 --> 16:38.539
Look at him. How embarrassing.
He's opening the door and everything.

16:38.622 --> 16:41.333
Does he also slice
pork cutlets for her at restaurants?

16:42.459 --> 16:48.590
♪ A different kind of reality ♪

16:49.633 --> 16:53.470
♪ I dream of loving in the night ♪

16:53.554 --> 16:56.557
♪ And loving seems all right… ♪

16:57.808 --> 16:58.767
Get in.

16:58.851 --> 17:01.353
♪ Fantasy ♪

17:08.986 --> 17:11.071
♪ All you need is love ♪

17:11.155 --> 17:12.740
♪ Ba-ba-da-ba-da ♪

17:12.823 --> 17:14.992
♪ All you need is love ♪

17:15.075 --> 17:17.161
♪ Ba-ba-da-ba-da ♪

17:18.495 --> 17:19.329
Hmm.

17:20.414 --> 17:23.125
You just have to remember
who that girl's parents are,

17:23.208 --> 17:24.835
and the future becomes clear.

17:24.918 --> 17:27.129
I can see it already.

17:28.088 --> 17:31.884
That whole family just has
no… no concept of decency at all.

17:31.967 --> 17:32.968
Don't you think?

17:33.052 --> 17:34.344
Boop!

17:34.428 --> 17:38.557
Fine, so you bought the tree,
but you can't take credit for the rock.

17:38.640 --> 17:41.018
You just wrote your name
on public property.

17:41.101 --> 17:42.936
When you get down to it,

17:43.020 --> 17:45.481
Ae-sun doesn't even deserve to be deputy.

17:45.564 --> 17:48.192
Who does she think she is?
She knows nothing at all.

17:48.275 --> 17:51.487
Hey, Captain. Are you actually
running on anything or what?

17:51.570 --> 17:52.404
What?

17:52.488 --> 17:55.157
Because it seems like you're running
just to trash-talk your opponent.

17:57.409 --> 18:00.037
It's not talking trash.

18:00.120 --> 18:02.081
It's just discussing morality.

18:02.164 --> 18:05.584
The people have a right to know
who their candidates are, don't they?

18:05.667 --> 18:07.252
BADA SEAFOOD HOUSE

18:07.336 --> 18:10.172
I can't believe that scumbag
brought your kids into this.

18:10.839 --> 18:13.967
-It's outrageous.
-Sang-gil crossed the line.

18:14.718 --> 18:16.095
You need to fight back.

18:17.304 --> 18:20.349
If you keep talking like that,
Ae-sun will have to respond.

18:20.432 --> 18:23.268
She's been holding back
because she's got some class.

18:23.352 --> 18:25.479
-But if push comes to shove…
-Oh yes. That's right.

18:25.562 --> 18:28.232
…I imagine she'd have
a thing or two to say about you.

18:28.732 --> 18:32.778
I remember his father
back during the occupation.

18:33.278 --> 18:36.240
He couldn't wait to take on
a Japanese name!

18:38.700 --> 18:40.077
Funny.

18:40.661 --> 18:43.330
But you're not gonna find
any dirt on our side.

18:43.956 --> 18:44.790
After all,

18:45.582 --> 18:48.585
I make contributions to our government,

18:49.169 --> 18:50.796
But Oh Ae-sun, well,

18:51.380 --> 18:54.508
I'm pretty sure she's never
given as much as a dime to charity.

18:56.802 --> 18:59.429
Politics is a land
of dog shit anyway.

18:59.513 --> 19:02.641
If you have to roll in it,
better to have black fur than white.

19:02.724 --> 19:05.477
If you roll in crap,
you get dirty all the same.

19:06.228 --> 19:07.104
Black fur or not.

19:07.187 --> 19:09.273
I'll win, but I won't change.

19:10.357 --> 19:13.735
Oh, that's our Oh Ae-sun,
just as proud as ever.

19:13.819 --> 19:16.738
You're not giving out soap.
You're not feeding them pork.

19:16.822 --> 19:18.323
You're not even playing dirty.

19:19.074 --> 19:21.285
Well, you might just lose. You might lose.

19:22.202 --> 19:24.371
Ae-sun, it's only fair.

19:24.454 --> 19:27.624
The villagers have a right to know
exactly who Sang-gil is.

19:27.708 --> 19:30.210
And he already crossed the line
to attack you.

19:30.294 --> 19:32.462
You may as well get him back too!

19:32.546 --> 19:36.967
Hey, a caterpillar will get eaten
if it stays in its cocoon too long.

19:37.050 --> 19:40.387
If that caterpillar struggles
and breaks out of its shell,

19:40.470 --> 19:42.139
it flies away a butterfly.

19:42.222 --> 19:45.976
You need to jump over the hurdle
before you fight your way out, Ae-sun.

19:46.727 --> 19:50.981
♪ Clock strikes upon the hour
And the sun begins to fade ♪

19:51.064 --> 19:53.525
♪ Still enough time to figure out ♪

19:53.609 --> 19:56.737
♪ How to chase Ae-sun away ♪

19:56.820 --> 19:58.989
♪ She's done all right up till now ♪

20:00.073 --> 20:02.951
♪ But I'll win reelection anyhow ♪

20:03.035 --> 20:05.287
♪ And when the night falls upon us ♪

20:05.829 --> 20:07.331
♪ Bu Sang-gil calls ♪

20:07.414 --> 20:08.999
♪ Da, da, da, da! ♪

20:09.082 --> 20:11.335
♪ Oh, if you wanna vote for me ♪

20:11.418 --> 20:13.795
♪ You can't find any dirt ♪

20:13.879 --> 20:15.047
Stop it, jeez!

20:15.130 --> 20:17.549
I'm not voting for someone
who ruins my appetite!

20:20.177 --> 20:21.511
Are those noodles coming?

20:21.595 --> 20:23.263
Mr. Gu, I think you'd sing better.

20:23.347 --> 20:25.724
He's always on his wife's case, isn't he?

20:27.976 --> 20:30.604
What's taking you so long
to cook those noodles?

20:31.897 --> 20:33.315
You're walking home tonight.

20:33.815 --> 20:35.651
You're not allowed in my car, understand?

20:35.734 --> 20:37.069
Hey, Bu Sang-gil,

20:37.694 --> 20:40.155
isn't it a bit ironic
your last name means "deputy?"

20:40.239 --> 20:42.824
Maybe you should just accept
that no matter where you go,

20:42.908 --> 20:44.743
you'll always be second fiddle.

20:47.996 --> 20:50.040
-What?
-Are you even voting for me?

20:50.123 --> 20:52.417
Or did you just come here
to make trouble or what?

20:52.501 --> 20:54.002
Is this 'cause I didn't get you a soda?

20:54.086 --> 20:57.130
Hey, if you do end up losing,
here's some advice.

20:57.214 --> 20:58.382
Why would I lose?

20:58.465 --> 21:01.843
Do you have any idea how much I've spent
on pork and noodles already, hmm?

21:01.927 --> 21:04.388
Don't settle for anything less
than deputy chief.

21:04.471 --> 21:06.348
It's like when you're watching Jeopardy,

21:06.431 --> 21:08.767
and someone gets out ahead
only to finish last.

21:09.268 --> 21:11.645
There's nothing more pathetic, is there?

21:11.728 --> 21:13.939
Spare yourself and finish second at least.

21:14.439 --> 21:15.565
-Hey!
-"Hey"?

21:15.649 --> 21:17.651
Did you just "hey" me?

21:17.734 --> 21:19.444
Where the hell are those noodles?

21:21.613 --> 21:23.615
You can vote for Oh Ae-sun if you want.

21:24.992 --> 21:26.576
FROM BU SANG-GIL, CANDIDATE 1

21:26.660 --> 21:30.247
But no matter how smart the Oh family is
or how undeserving the Bu family may be,

21:30.998 --> 21:33.875
there's no woman chief anywhere in Korea.

21:33.959 --> 21:36.628
-No, of course not.
-Wow. A box of cigarettes each?

21:36.712 --> 21:39.464
There's more?
I wish every day was election day.

21:40.882 --> 21:43.468
Who can stand in the way of a typhoon?

21:43.969 --> 21:46.555
Democracy is just data.

21:47.055 --> 21:48.682
That's how it goes.

21:49.850 --> 21:51.351
I vote Bu Sang-gil!

21:51.435 --> 21:54.146
-I'll drink to that! Drink!
-Raise a glass.

21:54.229 --> 21:56.023
Here, pour me some.

21:56.940 --> 21:58.525
Yeah, that's it.

21:59.192 --> 22:01.570
-Who's your chief?
-Mr. Bu!

22:01.653 --> 22:04.364
-Who's your chief?
-Mr. Bu!

22:04.448 --> 22:07.367
-Who is your chief?
-Mr. Bu!

22:10.954 --> 22:14.333
Lucky you.
I hope you're the chief till you die.

22:14.916 --> 22:18.754
What can I say?
Indecency seems to run in the Oh family.

22:18.837 --> 22:20.714
Just have a look at my own daughters.

22:20.797 --> 22:22.883
Hyeon-suk, which stands for
"wise" and "enlightened,"

22:22.966 --> 22:23.925
and Jeong-suk,

22:24.843 --> 22:26.970
which stands for "silent."

22:27.054 --> 22:29.890
Oh, he's a damn fool
if there ever was one.

22:37.522 --> 22:38.440
I have…

22:39.983 --> 22:43.653
I have absolutely nothing
in my past to be ashamed of, Mi-suk.

22:45.113 --> 22:47.199
Life's a bitch, huh?

22:47.282 --> 22:51.036
It's always so difficult
to get anything done.

22:51.703 --> 22:53.914
You can sell everything
in the display case

22:53.997 --> 22:55.791
and still wind up with nothing.

22:58.168 --> 23:02.172
There's hardly any money to be made from
a real estate office on a tiny island.

23:02.255 --> 23:06.551
I thought that helping out
the Olympics Committee was my big break,

23:07.135 --> 23:09.763
but those haenyeo are so stubborn.

23:10.889 --> 23:12.057
You know what I'm like.

23:12.140 --> 23:14.309
-Mm.
-I'm a softie.

23:14.893 --> 23:18.021
Mi-suk, I swear… I'll take care of it.

23:18.939 --> 23:20.607
I'm your guy.

23:21.149 --> 23:24.319
I'm practically a shoo-in
for reelection now.

23:25.612 --> 23:26.488
Really?

23:26.571 --> 23:29.324
You'd take care of everything
just like that?

23:29.408 --> 23:31.785
I wouldn't even have to pay
a fee or anything, Bu Sang-gil?

23:31.868 --> 23:32.911
30%.

23:33.787 --> 23:34.621
What?

23:34.704 --> 23:35.789
30/70 split.

23:38.375 --> 23:40.836
Oh, all right.

23:40.919 --> 23:43.713
After all,
cooperation makes the world go round.

23:43.797 --> 23:45.966
Mi-suk, I'm your guy.

23:46.675 --> 23:49.177
Dodong-ri's own Bu Sang-gil.

23:49.886 --> 23:50.762
Mi-suk.

23:52.013 --> 23:53.265
Listen.

23:53.348 --> 23:57.519
I may have money, but I don't have
enough romance in my life.

23:58.687 --> 24:00.856
I'm really quite a lonely guy.

24:05.068 --> 24:06.653
You don't have to be shy.

24:09.197 --> 24:10.991
Oh, I'm not.

24:12.159 --> 24:13.869
Come on.

24:14.744 --> 24:18.707
You don't think I'm offering
to help you for the money, do you?

24:19.791 --> 24:23.253
Well, if it's not for the money,
then what's it for?

24:26.465 --> 24:27.799
Don't make that face.

24:29.759 --> 24:30.844
What face?

24:32.846 --> 24:35.348
It's the Olympics, after all.

24:35.432 --> 24:38.268
Walls are falling down all over the world,

24:38.351 --> 24:40.770
even in the Soviet Union.

24:41.313 --> 24:43.273
We could just break down the wall

24:44.774 --> 24:46.151
in between us two.

24:51.865 --> 24:53.950
Stop drinking.
You'll ruin your liver.

24:54.993 --> 24:55.827
Oh.

24:56.411 --> 25:00.248
But the quickest way to a man's heart
is through his stomach.

25:04.377 --> 25:07.047
Perhaps this isn't just a piece of fish

25:07.130 --> 25:10.634
but a trap for my stomach,
and my heart has taken the bait.

25:11.343 --> 25:12.677
Maybe.

25:13.595 --> 25:14.429
Oh, thank you.

25:15.180 --> 25:19.392
These abalones are helping my heart
come out of its shell.

25:23.396 --> 25:25.148
Shut up and eat your shrimp.

25:26.858 --> 25:30.946
Your shrimp is really sending
the blood rushing to my… "muscle."

25:31.029 --> 25:32.739
You're so dirty!

25:32.822 --> 25:35.033
Wait, wait, I'm talking about…
It's my heart.

25:36.117 --> 25:38.370
I mean my heart.
The blood's rushing to my heart.

25:39.204 --> 25:41.414
Oh my God, you're such a clown.

25:41.498 --> 25:42.958
Oh! You're awful!

25:48.046 --> 25:49.172
Hey, listen.

25:51.299 --> 25:52.884
I thought this was just dinner.

25:54.803 --> 25:57.055
Why are you tormenting my lonely heart?

25:57.138 --> 25:59.099
Huh?

26:00.684 --> 26:03.478
-You're a naughty girl, aren't you?
-That tickles.

26:04.938 --> 26:06.481
Disgusting.

26:06.565 --> 26:09.276
Is this how you think
a village chief should act?

26:10.694 --> 26:14.281
You need to jump over the hurdle
before you fight your way out, Ae-sun.

26:16.324 --> 26:17.450
Oh my.

26:17.534 --> 26:19.744
Wait, where are you going?

26:20.412 --> 26:22.956
Damn it, what the hell
did you come in here for?

26:24.249 --> 26:27.586
Well, well, well, if it isn't
"Mr. Snitch-for-the-government."

26:27.669 --> 26:31.006
God, meongge guts are less gross than you.

26:31.631 --> 26:33.800
Who the hell are you
to judge me?

26:33.883 --> 26:38.138
What I do in private
is none of your goddamn business!

26:38.221 --> 26:41.683
Well, we work here. Remember? Moron.

26:41.766 --> 26:44.811
While you were telling that woman
the quickest way to a man's heart,

26:44.894 --> 26:47.022
she was cracking
your wallet open like meongge.

26:48.523 --> 26:50.483
Why were you
eavesdropping on us?

26:50.984 --> 26:52.777
-Why?
-I just realized.

26:53.278 --> 26:54.904
You're only village chief

26:54.988 --> 26:57.407
so you can massage
the feet of another man's wife!

26:59.159 --> 27:00.577
How dare you speak to me like that!

27:01.411 --> 27:04.247
Whatever your reasons,
you sure can't be chief anymore.

27:09.753 --> 27:12.213
Why can't I be chief though? Tell me.

27:12.297 --> 27:14.049
You're like a stray dog who goes around

27:14.132 --> 27:16.885
sticking his nose
into everyone's business.

27:16.968 --> 27:19.638
Are you really surprised eventually
people would get fed up with you?

27:19.721 --> 27:24.643
Yeah, we wouldn't even feed rotten rice
to a mutt like you, Sang-gil.

27:24.726 --> 27:28.313
But you want us to make you chief?
We have had it with your crap!

27:31.232 --> 27:32.984
How dare you. Really?

27:34.069 --> 27:36.863
You don't even… you don't even know!

27:36.946 --> 27:39.407
You don't have a clue
what really happened.

27:40.033 --> 27:43.161
All she said was that
her feet were asleep, okay?

27:43.244 --> 27:46.331
Yeah, right.
While your poor wife is aching all over.

27:46.956 --> 27:48.124
Some role model.

27:48.208 --> 27:50.960
Dragging Ae-sun's family into the race.

27:51.044 --> 27:53.254
So her son is a bit of a troublemaker.

27:53.338 --> 27:54.798
Does that make her one too?

27:55.674 --> 27:57.550
My son is smart in his own way.

27:57.634 --> 27:59.511
So what? What now, Ae-sun?

27:59.594 --> 28:01.680
What'll you do? Are you gonna tell on me?

28:02.555 --> 28:05.266
Naturally, naturally,
we will tell everyone and rat you out.

28:05.350 --> 28:07.560
We'll tell everyone,
and Ae-sun will be chief.

28:07.644 --> 28:08.645
That's right.

28:08.728 --> 28:09.896
Is that a fact?

28:10.563 --> 28:12.065
Is that the way you wanna win?

28:13.149 --> 28:14.275
People have a right

28:15.360 --> 28:16.319
to know who we are.

28:16.986 --> 28:20.949
It's not talking trash.
It's just discussing morality.

28:21.533 --> 28:23.702
Everyone has the right to know
their candidates, right?

28:23.785 --> 28:25.453
That's what you said, isn't it?

28:25.537 --> 28:28.206
-Oh, Ae-sun!
-Oh.

28:30.041 --> 28:32.127
You little…

28:37.716 --> 28:39.300
You shouldn't have.

28:39.384 --> 28:40.802
THE 7TH DODONG-RI CHIEF, OH AE-SUN

28:40.885 --> 28:42.011
Oh my!

28:42.095 --> 28:46.808
Ae-sun! Oh Ae-sun!
Oh Ae-sun! Oh Ae-sun!

28:46.891 --> 28:48.935
Ae-sun gave it
her best shot once again.

28:49.018 --> 28:50.353
Oh, look!

28:50.895 --> 28:52.814
Wow, the school lent this to us?

28:52.897 --> 28:55.233
They only use it
for sports day once a year.

28:55.316 --> 28:56.151
Wow.

28:56.234 --> 28:58.528
She hit the bull's-eye
right in the middle.

28:59.028 --> 29:01.072
-That day, Jeju Island…
-Chief!

29:01.156 --> 29:03.783
-…got its first-ever female village chief.
-Hey, Chief.

29:03.867 --> 29:05.493
Chief! Oh, hey!

29:05.577 --> 29:06.661
Uh, yes?

29:06.745 --> 29:09.122
-Look, the rice cake is here.
-Oh, bring it out.

29:09.748 --> 29:13.209
-Chief Oh, we're out of makgeolli.
-Oh, really?

29:14.210 --> 29:16.504
Chief Oh, any more blankets?

29:16.588 --> 29:17.797
-Uh-huh!
-Chief!

29:18.548 --> 29:22.177
It's the school asking if you can return
the banner by sports day, if that's okay?

29:23.678 --> 29:25.889
It pulled
at her heartstrings.

29:30.101 --> 29:33.813
Many years later, when
Mom joined Lim Young-woong's fan club,

29:33.897 --> 29:36.691
her username was Chief Oh.

29:39.819 --> 29:40.695
Hey, Chief Oh!

29:41.780 --> 29:44.407
Come over here and have a taste of this!
You have first dibs!

29:44.991 --> 29:45.867
Okay.

29:46.826 --> 29:48.036
Okay!

29:57.629 --> 29:59.672
-These are ready.
-Okay.

30:05.220 --> 30:07.180
There she is!

30:07.263 --> 30:09.057
THE 5TH AND 6TH FISHING CO-OP CHIEF
BU SANG-GIL

30:09.140 --> 30:11.768
Here, eat, eat, eat, eat.
I made so much.

30:19.108 --> 30:20.360
One more time!

30:22.946 --> 30:24.572
You serving meat at this thing?

30:25.281 --> 30:26.908
Or are you too goddamn cheap?

30:26.991 --> 30:30.829
Goodness. What's the point
of sitting here all angry?

30:30.912 --> 30:33.623
Why would I miss
my successor's inauguration ceremony?

30:33.706 --> 30:35.792
She doesn't know anything
about being chief.

30:35.875 --> 30:37.585
She needs all the advice she can get.

30:37.669 --> 30:41.589
Well, if you weren't here,
you'd seem a small man indeed.

30:41.673 --> 30:44.050
For your information, I have resigned.

30:44.551 --> 30:46.177
I stepped down on my own accord.

30:47.178 --> 30:50.849
You know the 80-year-old grandpa
who runs the convenience store?

30:52.225 --> 30:55.186
He's never said more than
two words to me before,

30:55.270 --> 30:59.315
but the other day, he asked if I knew
about Sang-gil and the foot massage.

31:00.024 --> 31:04.529
Oh, come on. How many times
do I have to say her feet were asleep?

31:05.530 --> 31:07.699
I would have done the same for anyone.

31:20.420 --> 31:23.506
I'll be serving
my daughter-in-law the rest of my life.

31:24.048 --> 31:27.343
Everyone in the family
is a bigwig politician now.

31:27.427 --> 31:30.305
If Ae-sun is the chief,
her husband's the consort,

31:30.805 --> 31:32.765
and I'm sort of like the queen mother.

31:32.849 --> 31:36.102
Jeez. So, yet again,
she is completely lost in her delusions.

31:36.185 --> 31:38.813
Isn't she something else?
Ever since she met Gwan-sik,

31:38.897 --> 31:40.189
things turned around for her.

31:40.273 --> 31:43.192
I can't tell if you're showing off or not.

31:43.276 --> 31:44.777
Showing off?

31:45.278 --> 31:47.155
How's your daughter-in-law?

31:47.238 --> 31:48.364
Still a gambler, no?

31:48.948 --> 31:50.241
Gambler?

31:50.325 --> 31:52.201
Hurry! We're out of pajeon!

31:52.285 --> 31:55.371
-Jeez.
-The First Gentleman is super busy.

31:55.455 --> 31:57.081
Don't call him First Gentleman.

31:58.750 --> 32:01.294
Good lord, son,
do you have to wear that apron?

32:01.377 --> 32:02.754
-Hey, Ma?
-What?

32:02.837 --> 32:04.964
Can you make them a little bigger? Please?

32:05.048 --> 32:07.175
Why, that…

32:08.801 --> 32:10.470
Now he's pissing me off.

32:12.221 --> 32:15.558
I think I understand.
You're happy Ae-sun is the chief,

32:15.642 --> 32:17.352
but you're also not.

32:17.435 --> 32:18.770
What's so funny?

32:19.562 --> 32:22.398
I've never seen you before. You know me?

32:22.482 --> 32:24.067
Yes, Chief Oh is on it!

32:24.150 --> 32:25.485
I'll be right there!

32:30.114 --> 32:32.367
-Oh my goodness!
-Now what's wrong?

32:32.867 --> 32:35.161
Like you never saw
your mother-in-law at work?

32:35.244 --> 32:38.373
Is this revenge?
Your way of getting back at me?

32:38.873 --> 32:41.084
Please, I'm not talking about that.

32:41.167 --> 32:42.001
Sure.

32:42.085 --> 32:45.254
Why are you making
my opponent's wife make our jeon?

32:49.801 --> 32:51.719
It's unbelievable, but true!

32:51.803 --> 32:53.846
Bu Sang-gil massaged her feet!

32:57.266 --> 33:00.937
Don't listen to them.
You know how an election can get.

33:01.854 --> 33:04.482
Everyone shares all the negative stories
they can think of,

33:05.066 --> 33:07.610
even about your great-great-grandfather.

33:08.111 --> 33:10.446
You should've told them
that I went dancing back then.

33:10.530 --> 33:12.323
No one ever found that out.

33:14.617 --> 33:15.785
I'm very sorry.

33:15.868 --> 33:20.289
I feel like I insulted you
discussing your sensitive issues.

33:21.207 --> 33:23.710
By the way, just between you and me,

33:24.627 --> 33:27.088
we took care of
the real estate lady on our end.

33:27.630 --> 33:29.257
I don't care about her.

33:29.340 --> 33:32.969
Gyeong-suk from the salon.
Mi-suk from the real estate office.

33:33.469 --> 33:34.971
Well, for such a tiny island,

33:35.054 --> 33:38.141
there are so many women
with such a bad taste in men.

33:39.225 --> 33:40.268
However,

33:41.144 --> 33:44.564
it's true that I'm the worst of them all.

33:48.234 --> 33:50.361
Listen, why don't you go home?

33:50.445 --> 33:53.197
People want to gossip.
You know, that's all.

33:53.281 --> 33:55.575
You think they're saying
I have no self-respect?

33:56.617 --> 34:02.373
No, I only meant that I feel awful
seeing you make jeon for our party.

34:02.457 --> 34:05.251
I want to, though,
because it's my prerogative.

34:05.960 --> 34:07.670
I have every right to be here.

34:09.714 --> 34:11.049
Besides, I voted for you.

34:12.967 --> 34:15.970
So, at the very least,
I think I deserve a drink

34:16.054 --> 34:17.722
that you pour me yourself.

34:21.392 --> 34:23.186
Yeong-ran, listen.

34:23.770 --> 34:27.356
When you go home,
no, until the day you die,

34:27.440 --> 34:30.234
tell your husband you voted for him, hmm?

34:31.736 --> 34:35.406
Hey, Yeong-ran,
who did you vote for?

34:45.416 --> 34:47.085
Why can't you answer me?

34:47.668 --> 34:48.920
You didn't vote for me.

34:49.003 --> 34:51.547
Come on, now.
What are you picking on Mom for?

34:51.631 --> 34:53.341
Hey, you little brat.

34:53.424 --> 34:55.468
Don't you disrespect me. What do you know?

34:56.177 --> 34:58.387
You don't know jack shit about anything.

35:03.101 --> 35:07.188
Why? Why? Tell me why.

35:07.271 --> 35:09.690
Why did the governor come today?

35:09.774 --> 35:13.236
Why would the governor come
to a village chief's inauguration?

35:13.319 --> 35:14.779
He didn't come to mine!

35:14.862 --> 35:16.114
The governor?

35:16.197 --> 35:18.366
Gwan-sik got a plaque of honor.

35:19.033 --> 35:20.868
That's why the governor attended.

35:20.952 --> 35:22.662
For jumping into the water?

35:23.287 --> 35:26.499
If I saw someone drowning,
I would jump in a hundred times.

35:27.083 --> 35:29.210
I'd get a hundred commendations!

35:29.293 --> 35:33.756
Wow. I heard there was a reward,
that they're getting a trip and stuff.

35:34.465 --> 35:35.424
That's right.

35:36.259 --> 35:38.052
The governor likes Gwan-sik.

35:39.011 --> 35:40.304
He really does.

35:42.557 --> 35:43.933
Of course he does.

35:45.643 --> 35:47.103
Of course he does.

35:47.186 --> 35:49.313
Why? Why?

35:50.273 --> 35:55.069
Why does everyone here just love
that little stupid punk? Why?

35:55.153 --> 35:57.655
GOVERNOR HWANG IN-SU
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR INAUGURATION

36:01.450 --> 36:04.912
If your grandma were alive,
she would've drowned her in red beans.

36:17.842 --> 36:20.011
Come on, let's dance the night away!

36:22.805 --> 36:26.475
My God. What's going on over here?
Come on!

36:26.976 --> 36:29.812
You ought to be ashamed of yourself!
We're going home!

36:35.985 --> 36:38.362
Dad, you have to stop her. She's so drunk!

36:42.700 --> 36:46.204
Goodness. She loves Busan, doesn't she?

36:46.954 --> 36:48.623
She calls herself a bookworm.

36:48.706 --> 36:51.500
You're no bookworm! Just a lousy dancer!

36:59.383 --> 37:01.093
Do you see
what she's doing with that pole?

37:01.177 --> 37:03.930
Go throw those red beans at her.

37:12.188 --> 37:13.189
Dad!

37:13.272 --> 37:15.608
Leave her alone.
Let her have her fun, kid.

37:17.151 --> 37:19.820
I'm so glad I have a dog.

37:19.904 --> 37:21.906
Oh, where is he?

37:22.782 --> 37:24.408
Let's go, Duraengi.

37:24.492 --> 37:26.452
Here, Duraengi. Here, boy.

37:27.286 --> 37:28.537
Let's go, honey.

37:29.288 --> 37:30.414
That's a good boy.

37:42.134 --> 37:42.969
Hey, Dad.

37:43.678 --> 37:44.887
I can take her.

37:45.471 --> 37:46.305
You happy?

37:47.932 --> 37:48.891
Yeah.

37:49.558 --> 37:50.643
I am.

37:51.644 --> 37:54.647
I'm so happy.

37:56.315 --> 37:59.694
You're not a vice president,
a deputy director, or a deputy chief.

38:00.486 --> 38:01.821
You're chief, period.

38:04.365 --> 38:06.367
You know, it's strange.

38:06.450 --> 38:10.663
Even though I've finally lost the "deputy"
from my title after 30 years,

38:12.206 --> 38:15.042
the person I wanna tell the most
isn't here.

38:20.715 --> 38:25.428
I wouldn't say I wanna go back
to my childhood, because it was horrible,

38:26.846 --> 38:29.473
but if there were any way I could go back,

38:32.059 --> 38:33.477
I think I would.

38:35.271 --> 38:39.442
If only for the chance
to hold my mother's hand one more time.

38:40.568 --> 38:43.571
Do you know the reason
why I became the vice president now?

38:44.363 --> 38:46.532
It's so that I can be chief in the future.

38:46.615 --> 38:48.451
It's like diving.

38:48.534 --> 38:50.911
You start in the shallow water,
then go deeper.

38:52.747 --> 38:55.708
Little by little, I'll build experience
and become chief one day.

38:55.791 --> 38:58.627
There's no one on the island
more powerful than a chief.

38:59.670 --> 39:02.840
Even Auntie Gyeong-ja never forgets
to pay her loans back.

39:02.923 --> 39:07.178
Okay, one day, you'll be chief
so I can be the chief's mother.

39:07.762 --> 39:09.764
Will you make rice cake when it happens?

39:10.556 --> 39:14.268
I'm going to make so much rice cake,
it'll pile up as high as a mountain.

39:14.352 --> 39:17.229
-You'd be happy?
-Uh-huh. I'd be happy.

39:17.313 --> 39:18.397
Very much so.

39:20.441 --> 39:21.734
Actually, I'm holding back.

39:22.401 --> 39:25.571
I'm saving up all my happiness
for when that day comes.

39:28.449 --> 39:30.910
Go on, take as much as you want.

39:30.993 --> 39:34.455
I want everyone to know how happy I am.
I'm not holding back.

39:36.665 --> 39:38.334
-Ooh!
-Go on.

39:38.417 --> 39:41.837
-Double portions for everyone.
-Oh, goodness, look.

39:42.463 --> 39:43.422
Oh my.

39:45.257 --> 39:48.302
With these nets,
you supported me when my mom couldn't.

39:48.886 --> 39:51.180
Now she needs you
to brag about me for her.

39:51.263 --> 39:53.432
-Oh my.
-Oh, goodness.

39:53.516 --> 39:57.478
You must've had a lot of rice.
Why did you make so much?

39:58.062 --> 39:59.730
This is Gwang-rye's doing.

39:59.814 --> 40:01.816
Thank you, Gwang-rye, for the rice!

40:02.316 --> 40:03.526
Oh my.

40:04.360 --> 40:05.194
Gwang-rye.

40:05.820 --> 40:10.157
If you could only see your daughter now.
Grown-up and the village chief.

40:11.158 --> 40:13.202
Remember when she was ten years old?

40:13.828 --> 40:16.414
I can still see her wearing
her funeral dress.

40:16.997 --> 40:18.332
Poor dear.

40:18.416 --> 40:20.709
I wondered if she'd make it.

40:20.793 --> 40:24.088
Who knew that not only
would she make it, but she would thrive?

40:24.171 --> 40:27.383
If Gwang-rye were with us,
she'd drum and play

40:27.466 --> 40:29.885
all around Mount Hallasan with us today.

40:29.969 --> 40:33.180
You had to dig out the frozen ground
with your tiny, little hand

40:33.264 --> 40:34.974
and bury your heart in it.

40:35.057 --> 40:37.268
Your harvesting season has come at last.

40:39.228 --> 40:42.148
Gwang-rye's persimmon tree
is growing well, isn't it?

40:42.648 --> 40:44.817
Growing tall and strong.

40:44.900 --> 40:48.112
It was now fall,
the season of harvest,

40:49.071 --> 40:53.033
when all kinds of fruits
were ripening on the vine.

41:06.297 --> 41:09.592
Their harvest was beginning
to overflow the basket.

41:11.719 --> 41:16.307
But depending on where we were,
the sun bathed us in a different light.

41:23.522 --> 41:25.566
Oh, look.

41:34.867 --> 41:35.868
Why, uh…

41:36.952 --> 41:39.413
-Huh?
-Why are you still in the front seat?

41:39.497 --> 41:40.539
Oh.

41:41.582 --> 41:42.625
You know,

41:44.335 --> 41:45.794
it's fun sometimes.

41:48.589 --> 41:49.673
Thanks again.

41:51.467 --> 41:53.260
She can't stand seeing me in here.

41:53.344 --> 41:55.054
Oh, that mean girl you told me about?

41:55.137 --> 41:55.971
Yeah.

41:56.055 --> 41:56.889
Yeong-beom!

42:02.645 --> 42:03.562
Yeong-beom!

42:16.408 --> 42:18.661
Let me know
if you would like anything else, okay?

42:20.246 --> 42:22.081
You also don't know whose car that is?

42:22.164 --> 42:24.708
Something's up with Yang Geum-myeong.
Think about it.

42:25.376 --> 42:26.710
Don't say stuff like that.

42:27.628 --> 42:29.630
She may be poor, but she still has class.

42:29.713 --> 42:32.216
And, Ye-rim,
stop taking her side.

42:32.299 --> 42:35.761
Geum-myeong is never nice to you.
Why give her the benefit of the doubt?

42:36.345 --> 42:37.888
It's how she shows displeasure.

42:37.972 --> 42:39.431
In her own twisted way.

42:39.515 --> 42:41.100
What do you mean?

42:42.560 --> 42:45.563
My dad and I talked a bit about
Geum-myeong the other day.

42:45.646 --> 42:48.899
He said it's a big fish
in a little pond situation.

42:48.983 --> 42:51.652
She's used to being the best
at everything back at home.

42:51.735 --> 42:54.572
However, up here in Seoul,
she's really not that special.

42:56.156 --> 42:58.117
She must feel more inferior every day.

42:58.784 --> 43:01.078
Dad says I should be
the bigger person and let her be.

43:01.161 --> 43:02.454
That's what "class" is.

43:02.538 --> 43:03.372
Okay.

43:05.374 --> 43:07.376
But why would she act that way with you?

43:08.002 --> 43:09.461
Her GPA is higher than yours.

43:09.545 --> 43:11.547
By 0.2. Just by 0.2 points.

43:11.630 --> 43:13.048
-She's taller.
-By two centimeters.

43:13.132 --> 43:14.133
Also,

43:16.051 --> 43:17.886
have you memorized everything about her?

43:19.054 --> 43:20.889
-What do you mean?
-Doesn't matter.

43:20.973 --> 43:22.433
No, tell me. "Doesn't matter" what?

43:23.434 --> 43:24.268
I just meant

43:25.311 --> 43:27.813
Geum-myeong was chosen
to study in Japan first.

43:27.896 --> 43:31.191
If she hadn't passed it up, you wouldn't
have gotten the opportunity. Because of--

43:31.275 --> 43:33.611
If it were up to me,
I'd have chosen her as well.

43:34.194 --> 43:36.113
My family can afford to send me abroad.

43:36.196 --> 43:39.617
It's only natural they would choose
someone from a less fortunate background.

43:39.700 --> 43:40.534
Ye-rim.

43:40.618 --> 43:42.620
Geum-myeong's family is just fine.

43:42.703 --> 43:44.872
-Her father is a captain.
-Of a fishing boat!

43:44.955 --> 43:46.582
Why are you defending her?

43:48.000 --> 43:49.668
That's what class is about.

43:52.463 --> 43:53.422
I'm not hungry.

43:58.093 --> 43:59.762
She dumped you, didn't she?

43:59.845 --> 44:02.264
What is that foreign car?
What is it? Tell me!

44:03.265 --> 44:05.184
You are just dying to know, aren't you?

44:05.267 --> 44:08.771
PRIVATE TUTORING BAN SPARKS ODDITIES
TUTORING EVEN TAKING PLACE IN MOVING CARS!

44:13.859 --> 44:15.694
23RD TYPHOON "PHYLLIS"
CAUTIONS IN FISHING TOWNS

44:15.778 --> 44:17.154
How are the waters today?

44:18.155 --> 44:20.616
No matter how bad
the water might be,

44:21.200 --> 44:22.660
my dad sails to sea.

44:24.912 --> 44:26.830
And it makes me nervous.

44:28.207 --> 44:29.458
-Bye.
-See you later.

44:29.541 --> 44:30.584
Be safe.

44:39.426 --> 44:41.804
-Let's roll.
-No.

44:41.887 --> 44:43.639
-What?
-What did I say about being polite?

44:43.722 --> 44:44.848
Shut the fuck up.

44:44.932 --> 44:47.309
Whoa! Don't say "shut the fuck."
It's "Jesus Christ."

44:47.393 --> 44:48.227
Ugh!

44:48.310 --> 44:51.021
You can't even spell "Wednesday."
Where did you learn to swear?

44:51.105 --> 44:52.439
Jesus!

44:55.442 --> 44:58.237
Jenny, do you know
how to spell "Wednesday"? Write it out.

44:58.320 --> 45:00.030
Write it out.

45:00.823 --> 45:02.574
Oh, goodness gracious.

45:02.658 --> 45:04.410
Why were you named "Jenny" anyway?

45:04.493 --> 45:07.329
Is it to make people think
you're American or something?

45:07.413 --> 45:09.581
If you were anyone else,
I'd have you fired.

45:09.665 --> 45:10.874
I'd have you worse than fired.

45:10.958 --> 45:12.584
Fire me, go ahead.

45:13.460 --> 45:15.337
Why haven't you fired me already?

45:15.421 --> 45:17.506
I heard none of your tutors
last more than a month.

45:17.589 --> 45:19.383
Yeah, I can't wait.

45:20.342 --> 45:21.719
Feet down!

45:33.772 --> 45:34.606
Hey, Jenny.

45:35.441 --> 45:37.401
You didn't memorize the vocab, did you?

45:38.068 --> 45:40.446
You just come to my house to eat,
don't you?

45:41.363 --> 45:44.366
Your housekeeper is good.
She can make food from anywhere.

45:45.075 --> 45:47.119
This is from Busan. Glass noodles.

45:47.202 --> 45:49.872
She just used our money
to impress people.

45:51.707 --> 45:54.710
You're such a brat.
That lady will quit, too, because of you.

45:55.711 --> 45:59.089
That lady has been here the longest.
Mom likes her, I guess.

46:00.132 --> 46:04.219
You know, it seems like people don't stay
at your house for a very long time.

46:05.053 --> 46:05.971
Why?

46:07.973 --> 46:08.891
Why?

46:11.977 --> 46:12.978
Also,

46:14.521 --> 46:18.400
I still don't understand
why I've never met your mother or father.

46:18.484 --> 46:20.319
So what? It's better that way.

46:20.903 --> 46:23.113
I'd like to see their faces at least once.

46:23.197 --> 46:25.657
Well, my mom's seen you.
That should be enough.

46:25.741 --> 46:27.451
What? She saw me? Where?

46:27.534 --> 46:28.619
Where was this?

46:28.702 --> 46:30.454
You stapled a picture to your résumé.

46:31.079 --> 46:34.708
Just hang around until your time's up.
I know you don't wanna be here anyway.

46:34.792 --> 46:36.043
You're here for the money.

46:36.126 --> 46:37.544
Well, aren't you a genius, Jenny.

46:38.128 --> 46:39.963
And, yes, I want to be paid.

46:40.047 --> 46:41.882
Ms. Yang, can't you fix your bangs

46:41.965 --> 46:43.967
or change where
you part your hair at least?

46:44.051 --> 46:45.844
You don't look like you're from Seoul.

46:46.345 --> 46:47.429
Fix them?

46:47.513 --> 46:49.681
Why are you so worried about my hairstyle?

46:50.390 --> 46:53.018
I mean, it's not like
you and I look that much alike.

46:53.101 --> 46:54.019
What?

46:54.102 --> 46:57.064
But… I am the sexier one.

46:57.147 --> 46:59.650
Sexy? Sexy?

47:00.526 --> 47:01.985
Here.

47:02.069 --> 47:04.071
That's a new vocab word. Spell it.

47:04.154 --> 47:06.532
Come on, that's easy. S-E--

47:06.615 --> 47:08.784
Enough.

47:09.451 --> 47:11.078
-S-E…
-I said, enough!

47:11.161 --> 47:12.871
That's all you're interested in, huh?

47:12.955 --> 47:14.998
Little brat, you.

47:25.884 --> 47:28.971
Just take what you're owed.
Don't take more than that.

47:31.098 --> 47:32.808
Your mother is getting to me.

47:34.142 --> 47:36.812
I'm tempted more
every single time, you know.

47:47.698 --> 47:48.782
Hello?

47:49.366 --> 47:50.200
Yeah, what?

47:50.284 --> 47:53.579
Just grab a handful.
Take double for teaching that brat.

47:55.205 --> 47:56.081
What?

47:59.126 --> 48:00.919
Mom's coming. She wants to see you.

48:01.753 --> 48:03.881
-What? Right now?
-Just go.

48:06.466 --> 48:07.467
Go now, girl.

48:32.951 --> 48:36.580
Yes, Ms. Yang,
that's real white porcelain.

48:38.457 --> 48:39.416
I see.

48:40.459 --> 48:42.002
I have everything now.

48:42.502 --> 48:45.047
I have blue porcelain,
and I have white as well.

48:45.839 --> 48:48.759
Everything.
Everything except a good education.

48:50.385 --> 48:51.803
W… wow.

48:51.887 --> 48:54.556
I have such deep regret
for my lack of education.

48:54.640 --> 48:56.850
I was hoping to be able
to live through my daughter,

48:56.934 --> 48:59.186
but she has my intellect, unfortunately.

49:02.314 --> 49:06.360
We'll raise her grades little by little.
Don't worry.

49:06.443 --> 49:08.487
Sadly, there's no time for that now.

49:09.237 --> 49:11.448
Life doesn't wait for anyone.
We all know that.

49:12.616 --> 49:13.450
Ah…

49:13.951 --> 49:17.245
Uh, then does that mean I'm fired?

49:17.329 --> 49:19.873
Jenny is very wealthy,
but she isn't that clever,

49:19.957 --> 49:22.626
while you are very smart
and not much else.

49:22.709 --> 49:24.670
So let's try work this out together.

49:26.296 --> 49:29.466
I'll set things up
and take care of everything.

49:29.549 --> 49:31.802
You just follow my lead and directions.

49:32.594 --> 49:35.931
It took us two years to find a tutor
that looked like our daughter.

49:36.014 --> 49:37.641
Her college exams are very soon.

49:38.225 --> 49:39.685
You should take the exams for her.

49:40.394 --> 49:42.729
That's what I'm demanding of you,
Ms. Yang.

49:54.783 --> 49:55.617
Uh…

49:57.119 --> 49:58.620
Uh…

50:01.248 --> 50:03.625
STUDENT ID
OH JENNY

50:03.709 --> 50:05.085
TEST IDENTIFICATION SLIP
OH JENNY

50:05.168 --> 50:07.504
If she gets into a top-three university,

50:07.587 --> 50:10.007
I'll buy you a 1,300-square-foot apartment

50:10.090 --> 50:12.592
and a 1,000-square-foot one
for other colleges.

50:20.976 --> 50:23.145
NOTICE
LIST OF APPROVED APPLICANTS FOR DORMS

50:25.188 --> 50:28.066
If her name
isn't here, she can't live in the dorms?

50:28.775 --> 50:29.776
No.

50:31.653 --> 50:33.864
Then a boarding house.

50:35.365 --> 50:36.575
How much is the rent there?

50:38.660 --> 50:39.578
A lot.

50:40.579 --> 50:41.913
It'll be expensive.

51:08.648 --> 51:09.483
What?

51:10.233 --> 51:11.359
Is he trying to fight?

51:12.152 --> 51:14.071
The eyes of the world
are upon us

51:14.154 --> 51:18.366
as a historical presidential election
unfolds today, on December 16th.

51:18.867 --> 51:20.911
It has been 16 years since our citizens

51:20.994 --> 51:23.288
have been able
to directly vote for the president.

51:23.371 --> 51:24.664
The atmosphere is solemn.

51:25.707 --> 51:30.253
They say the dorm selection is by lottery,
but I think there are backdoor deals.

51:30.337 --> 51:33.924
We all know supposedly
"clean" organizations can be shady.

51:34.007 --> 51:34.841
Right?

51:34.925 --> 51:36.343
…president of their choice.

51:36.426 --> 51:39.221
So… who are you voting for?

51:39.304 --> 51:41.348
…government has declared today
a temporary…

51:41.431 --> 51:43.809
I think we need to call
the military police.

51:43.892 --> 51:44.768
Excuse me?

51:44.851 --> 51:47.521
Why is there
a soldier outside the girls' dorm?

51:48.021 --> 51:49.523
The guys' dorms are nearby.

51:50.524 --> 51:53.360
Usually, when there's a break,
they come in and out.

51:55.862 --> 51:56.988
So who'd you vote for?

51:57.489 --> 51:59.950
…had given their all
to ask for each of their votes.

52:00.033 --> 52:02.285
You think they will be able
to arrest that guy?

52:07.249 --> 52:08.125
One.

52:08.667 --> 52:10.335
One, two, three.

52:11.461 --> 52:12.379
Oh!

52:16.925 --> 52:18.385
Sir, good to meet you again.

52:24.266 --> 52:27.060
Remember me, sir?
We met at the admission ceremony.

52:27.144 --> 52:29.729
I'm Park Yeong-beom,
and your daughter and I,

52:30.230 --> 52:31.148
we are friends.

52:36.987 --> 52:41.241
I recall on that day, I actually took
a few pictures of you guys.

52:45.453 --> 52:48.206
You were saying how
you took a plane to see Geum-myeong,

52:48.790 --> 52:49.875
then you took a bus.

52:50.375 --> 52:51.334
Yeah.

52:51.418 --> 52:52.460
What kind of friend?

52:53.336 --> 52:55.130
-Sir?
-I asked you a question.

52:56.506 --> 52:58.216
-Yeah?
-You're a friend of my daughter.

52:58.300 --> 53:00.594
Well, so tell me,
what kind of friend are you, boy?

53:00.677 --> 53:02.012
TEST IDENTIFICATION SLIP
OH JENNY

53:02.095 --> 53:02.929
Oh my God.

53:04.389 --> 53:06.057
Oh.

53:06.141 --> 53:07.726
I'm sorry, ma'am.

53:07.809 --> 53:09.895
This seems kind of risky.

53:09.978 --> 53:11.438
Tutoring is already illegal.

53:11.521 --> 53:14.441
In fact, every time I come here,
I get nervous.

53:14.983 --> 53:17.986
Takes nerve to earn
any money in this world, dear.

53:18.528 --> 53:20.822
You can't win if you risk nothing at all.

53:20.906 --> 53:22.949
If I get caught, I'd be expelled.

53:23.033 --> 53:25.035
That's why you're getting an apartment,

53:25.118 --> 53:27.829
to compensate you
for the risk of expulsion.

53:29.581 --> 53:32.250
Hold on, this exam is serious.

53:32.334 --> 53:34.336
You really think I can be Jenny?

53:35.212 --> 53:38.840
Whoever the proctor is,
I'll have greased their palm.

53:38.924 --> 53:41.593
I will arrange everything for you nicely

53:41.676 --> 53:44.054
so you won't have a reason
to be worried at all.

53:46.014 --> 53:50.602
Doesn't everyone make their money
by doing what they're good at?

53:50.685 --> 53:53.146
I will assist you
by doing what I'm good at.

53:54.022 --> 53:57.525
Isn't it right and honorable
to make a living using your talents?

53:58.735 --> 54:01.905
Just turn a blind eye this once
and take the apartment.

54:04.950 --> 54:06.243
There's just one thing--

54:06.326 --> 54:07.244
No, dear.

54:08.036 --> 54:09.746
I don't wanna hear it.

54:10.330 --> 54:14.251
Before you speak, think carefully about
what you stand to lose.

54:20.382 --> 54:24.010
You're running out of scholarship money,
and you have to leave the dorms.

54:24.511 --> 54:26.429
Forget about studying abroad.

54:26.513 --> 54:29.015
How… do you know all that?

54:29.516 --> 54:31.434
As I said, think carefully.

54:32.060 --> 54:37.023
Think of your parents who worked so hard
to get you to where you are, Ms. Yang.

54:37.107 --> 54:40.652
You're a fish
trying to get out of her pond,

54:41.152 --> 54:44.114
but that pond is getting dry. Hmm?

54:46.658 --> 54:47.784
Follow me.

54:48.785 --> 54:50.870
Hey. Go to your room.

54:56.918 --> 54:58.086
Young lady!

54:58.962 --> 55:00.297
Hey, young lady!

55:00.380 --> 55:01.840
Hey, young lady!

55:01.923 --> 55:02.924
Oh my.

55:03.842 --> 55:05.760
Did you just leave unit 908?

55:06.261 --> 55:08.346
Yes? What's this about?

55:08.430 --> 55:09.973
You ran so fast,

55:10.056 --> 55:12.100
I wasn't able to catch up.

55:12.684 --> 55:14.185
What? Why would I run?

55:14.269 --> 55:15.895
You stole something from that family?

55:16.521 --> 55:17.355
Huh?

55:18.231 --> 55:21.609
Come. Just give it here.
Don't make any more trouble.

55:24.571 --> 55:26.865
Um, is that what she said?

55:29.034 --> 55:31.619
I don't need
an answer from you right now.

55:32.287 --> 55:33.830
Just take these with you.

55:35.415 --> 55:38.835
Look at it as many times as you need,
then tell me your decision, okay?

55:40.003 --> 55:42.714
Nobody wants to be stuck
in a small pond, do they?

55:42.797 --> 55:45.300
It's just too sad to contemplate.

55:46.176 --> 55:47.052
Imagine, instead,

55:47.135 --> 55:50.138
how you'd be able to give
your mother and father the whole world.

55:50.221 --> 55:53.558
That poor father of yours.
Always riding his boat.

55:54.142 --> 55:56.853
He'll have to ride in that boat
for the rest of his life.

56:00.482 --> 56:01.566
I remember my father.

56:02.192 --> 56:04.944
He trusted his eldest son to pass the bar,

56:05.028 --> 56:08.031
and he was stuck tending his cows
until the day he died.

56:09.949 --> 56:12.619
When I think of my parents
and how they're struggling,

56:12.702 --> 56:14.579
there's nothing to think about here.

56:14.662 --> 56:17.916
What's better than earning an apartment
doing what I'm good at?

56:18.416 --> 56:20.543
Yes, that's what I wanna hear.

56:20.627 --> 56:22.837
I remember what my mom and dad taught me.

56:23.421 --> 56:24.255
What?

56:24.339 --> 56:27.717
I was taught it was better to fail a class
than cheat my way in.

56:28.385 --> 56:32.013
I was taught not to take money I found
but to report it instead.

56:32.097 --> 56:35.892
I know my parents wouldn't want me to live
as a fraud or a scammer.

56:35.975 --> 56:39.104
Huh? What exactly
are you trying to say to me?

56:39.187 --> 56:40.230
Just

56:40.814 --> 56:43.858
that if I take the test
and Jenny gets accepted somehow,

56:43.942 --> 56:45.819
then a girl like me won't, and

56:46.778 --> 56:49.280
I can't stand the idea
of taking it from her.

56:50.323 --> 56:51.991
If she found out about it,

56:52.742 --> 56:54.285
she would die of heartbreak.

56:55.161 --> 56:57.122
Yang Geum-myeong, listen to me.

56:57.789 --> 56:59.916
It's one thing
to stand for your principles

56:59.999 --> 57:01.751
when you have the proper means,

57:01.835 --> 57:05.004
but to do it when you have nothing
is simply recklessness.

57:05.088 --> 57:06.965
I'd say sending a girl
who can't even spell

57:07.048 --> 57:08.675
to an elite school would be reckless.

57:08.758 --> 57:10.593
Would you?

57:12.554 --> 57:13.721
I think you

57:14.347 --> 57:16.349
should let Jenny find out
what she's really good at.

57:17.183 --> 57:19.769
Isn't that the right and honorable thing
to do for Jenny?

57:20.728 --> 57:22.188
Yeah, I'd rather be a singer.

57:27.318 --> 57:28.570
I am leaving now.

57:28.653 --> 57:33.158
All you little fish
are exactly the same.

57:33.658 --> 57:35.285
You have nothing to your name,

57:35.368 --> 57:39.372
so all you have to live for is preserving
your pathetic sense of pride!

57:41.708 --> 57:43.460
Jenny was always a pain in the ass.

57:46.713 --> 57:48.798
I think I deserve a raise after all this.

58:06.149 --> 58:07.734
You know I'm not a thief.

58:07.817 --> 58:10.612
Oh yes, I know.
I'm just keeping out of that bully's way.

58:10.695 --> 58:13.156
All the cash in the world
can't buy my integrity.

58:16.701 --> 58:17.535
The ring?

58:18.286 --> 58:19.120
What?

58:19.204 --> 58:21.456
You know, the diamond ring.

58:35.970 --> 58:37.889
My parents always hoped…

58:38.890 --> 58:43.186
…that away from their arms,
my life would be rosy, easy, and carefree.

58:43.269 --> 58:44.604
Open up!

58:46.189 --> 58:47.482
Ma'am, open up!

58:48.274 --> 58:51.069
Hey, Jenny! Open the door, come on!

58:51.152 --> 58:52.862
I didn't steal anything!

58:54.531 --> 58:58.618
Hey! You know I'm not a thief! Open up!

58:59.619 --> 59:02.705
But the truth is,
the world away from their arms

59:03.331 --> 59:04.374
was a jungle.

01:01:51.541 --> 01:01:55.545
"IN THE HOPE THAT OUR ECHOES
WILL FLOW AND FLOW, UNTIL THEY REACH YOU."
